--- body ---
Version 2.1 simplifies the primary dialog to two grouped progress areas:
global verified-pack coverage and current-document progress. Main text shows
only useful state and estimates. Duration is written as “Durée estimée: median
(entre low et high)” and global completion as “Fin estimée vers time (entre
time et time)”. No estimate text is inserted when the fit is unavailable.

Long native silence is surfaced only when progress reaches 90% (reference
analysis) or 95% (finalisation). Diagnostic counters, cache/session details,
and native lexical statistics are behind a collapsed Details section.

Passing exact Zotero 10.0.1 evidence is in the last smoke arena recorded by
the session; package source is `bench/sdt-sitter/` and the delivered artifact
is `/home/haduong/sdt-pack-sitter-2.1.0.xpi`.

Follow-up 2.1.1: global finish time now uses the observed document-rate
distribution for documents lacking usable page/byte covariates. One atypical
document no longer suppresses the library-wide clock estimate.
